{"parentUuid":"e28ba33f-0198-445d-9ced-a55510296710","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/giladbarnea/dev/twilio-demo/vapi-poc/mvp2","sessionId":"a6f25fb8-e7a8-4411-b378-ad0f20e552d1","version":"2.0.36","gitBranch":"vapi","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Export the current conversation to XML format with message indices.\n\n## Usage\n\n- **With output path**: `/export path/to/output.xml` - saves to file\n- **Without path**: `/export` - copies to clipboard (macOS)\n\n## Implementation\n\nUse the conversations skill's parse.py script to export the current conversation.\n\nSteps:\n1. Locate the current conversation file from the session\n2. Run the conversations skill parser:\n   ```bash\n   /Users/giladbarnea/.local/bin/uv run --with=rich \\\n     /Users/giladbarnea/.claude/skills/conversations/scripts/parse.py \\\n     <conversation-path> --color never\n   ```\n3. If output path provided ($1), save to that file using `-o` flag\n4. If no output path, pipe to `pbcopy` for clipboard\n\nThe export includes:\n- XML tags with message indices: `<user-message i=\"1\">`, `<assistant-response i=\"2\">`\n- All user messages and assistant text responses\n- Excludes tool calls by default (use `-t` to include)\n"}]},"isMeta":true,"uuid":"2c58169e-4570-4a68-a49b-e292298ed551","timestamp":"2025-11-23T09:18:28.048Z"}
